Goods and Material Management Module - Architecture Overview

  Your Spring Boot application implements a complete procurement and inventory management system with event-driven inventory tracking. Here's how it works:

  Core Entities and Their Relationships

  1. Material (Master Data)
  - The foundation of the system - represents inventory items
  - Contains: SKU, material name, unit of measurement
  - Tracks all inventory movements through relationships

  2. Vendor (Master Data)
  - Supplier information
  - Linked to: Purchase Orders, GRNs, and Payables

  3. Intend (Indent) - Material Requisition
  - Employee creates a request for materials
  - Contains multiple IndentItems
  - Status flow: PENDING → ORDERED → ON_SITE/DELAYED/CANCELLED
  - Acts as the starting point of the procurement workflow

  4. Purchase Order
  - Created from an Indent or standalone
  - Links to: Vendor, Indent (optional), multiple PurchaseOrderItems
  - Status flow: DRAFT → APPROVED → SENT_TO_VENDOR → PARTIALLY_RECEIVED → FULLY_RECEIVED
  - Tracks ordered vs received quantities per item

  5. Goods Received Note (GRN)
  - Records actual receipt of materials from vendor
  - Links to: PurchaseOrder, Vendor, multiple GrnItems
  - Captures: delivery challan, invoice details
  - Triggers automatic inventory increase via events

  6. InventoryTransaction (Auto-generated)
  - Ledger of all inventory movements
  - Records: opening stock, quantity changed, closing stock
  - Types: GRN (increase), USE (decrease), TRANSFER (decrease), ADJUST
  - Created automatically by event listeners

  7. MaterialConsumption
  - Records materials used from stock
  - Types: USED_FROM_STOCK, TRANSFERRED
  - Triggers automatic inventory decrease via events

  8. SiteTransfer
  - Transfer materials between sites
  - Reduces inventory at source site
  - Status: PENDING → PARTIALLY_TRANSFERRED → COMPLETED
  - Triggers automatic inventory decrease via events

  9. Payable
  - Financial obligations to vendors
  - Linked to: Vendor, GRN
  - Tracks: amount recorded vs amount paid
  - Contract types available

  Event-Driven Inventory System

  The system uses Spring Application Events to automatically maintain inventory:

  InventoryEventListener listens for:
  1. GrnCreatedEvent → Creates INBOUND transactions
  2. MaterialConsumedEvent → Creates OUTBOUND (USE) transactions
  3. SiteTransferCreatedEvent → Creates OUTBOUND (TRANSFER) transactions

  This ensures inventory is always automatically updated when goods are received, consumed, or transferred.

  Complete Workflow - How to Use the System

  Step 1: Set Up Master Data

  Create Materials:
  POST /api/v1/materials
  {
    "sku": "MAT001",
    "materialName": "Portland Cement",
    "unit": "bag"
  }

  Create Vendors:
  POST /api/v1/vendors
  {
    "vendorName": "ABC Suppliers",
    "vendorEmail": "abc@suppliers.com",
    "vendorAddress": "123 Industrial Area"
  }

  Step 2: Requisition Process (Indent)

  Create an Indent:
  POST /api/v1/intends
  {
    "expectedOn": "2025-12-20T00:00:00",
    "remarks": "Materials for Block A construction",
    "items": [
      {
        "materialId": 1,
        "requestedQuantity": 100,
        "additionalSpecifications": "Grade 53",
        "remarks": "Urgent"
      }
    ]
  }

  View all indents:
  GET /api/v1/intends
  GET /api/v1/intends/{id}

  Step 3: Create Purchase Order

  From Indent or Standalone:
  POST /api/v1/purchase-orders
  {
    "vendorId": 1,
    "intendId": 1,  // Optional - links to indent
    "expectedDeliveryDate": "2025-12-18T00:00:00",
    "remarks": "Rush order",
    "items": [
      {
        "materialId": 1,
        "indentItemId": 1,  // Optional - links to indent item
        "orderedQuantity": 100,
        "unitPrice": 450.00,
        "remarks": "Grade 53 cement"
      }
    ]
  }

  Update PO Status:
  PATCH /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id}/status?status=APPROVED
  PATCH /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id}/status?status=SENT_TO_VENDOR

  Query Purchase Orders:
  GET /api/v1/purchase-orders                  # All POs
  GET /api/v1/purchase-orders/{id}            # Specific PO
  GET /api/v1/purchase-orders/vendor/{vendorId}
  GET /api/v1/purchase-orders/intend/{intendId}
  GET /api/v1/purchase-orders/status/APPROVED

  Step 4: Receive Goods (GRN)

  Create GRN when goods arrive:
  POST /api/v1/grns
  {
    "receivedOn": "2025-12-18T10:30:00",
    "vendorId": 1,
    "purchaseOrderId": 1,
    "deliveryChallanNumber": "DC-2025-001",
    "invoiceNumber": "INV-2025-001",
    "invoiceAmount": 45000.00,
    "items": [
      {
        "materialId": 1,
        "orderedQuantity": 100,
        "receivedQuantity": 95  // Partial delivery
      }
    ]
  }

  What happens automatically:
  - GrnCreatedEvent is published
  - InventoryEventListener creates InventoryTransaction records
  - Stock increases for each material
  - PurchaseOrderItem.receivedQuantity is updated
  - PO status updates to PARTIALLY_RECEIVED or FULLY_RECEIVED

  Query GRNs:
  GET /api/v1/grns                            # All GRNs
  GET /api/v1/grns/{id}
  GET /api/v1/grns/vendor/{vendorId}
  GET /api/v1/grns/date-range?startDate=2025-12-01T00:00:00&endDate=2025-12-31T23:59:59

  Step 5: Check Inventory

  View material with current stock:
  GET /api/v1/materials/{id}/stock
  Returns:
  {
    "id": 1,
    "sku": "MAT001",
    "materialName": "Portland Cement",
    "unit": "bag",
    "currentStock": 95
  }

  View inventory transactions:
  GET /api/v1/inventory-transactions/material/{materialId}
  GET /api/v1/inventory-transactions/type/GRN
  GET /api/v1/inventory-transactions/date-range?startDate=...&endDate=...

  Each transaction shows: opening stock → quantity changed → closing stock

  Step 6: Consume Materials

  Record material usage:
  POST /api/v1/material-consumptions
  {
    "consumptionDate": "2025-12-19T14:00:00",
    "materialId": 1,
    "quantity": 20,
    "consumptionType": "USED_FROM_STOCK",
    "details": "Used for Block A foundation work"
  }

  What happens automatically:
  - Stock validation occurs (throws InsufficientStockException if not enough)
  - MaterialConsumedEvent is published
  - InventoryTransaction created (negative quantity)
  - Stock decreases automatically

  Query consumptions:
  GET /api/v1/material-consumptions/material/{materialId}
  GET /api/v1/material-consumptions/type/USED_FROM_STOCK
  GET /api/v1/material-consumptions/date-range?startDate=...&endDate=...

  Step 7: Transfer Between Sites

  Create site transfer:
  POST /api/v1/site-transfers
  {
    "issueDate": "2025-12-20T09:00:00",
    "receivingSite": "Site B - Project Phase 2",
    "items": [
      {
        "materialId": 1,
        "sentQuantity": 30,
        "remarks": "Transfer for Site B requirements"
      }
    ]
  }

  What happens automatically:
  - Stock validation occurs
  - SiteTransferCreatedEvent published
  - InventoryTransaction created (negative quantity)
  - Stock decreases at source site

  Update transfer status:
  PATCH /api/v1/site-transfers/{id}/status?status=COMPLETED

  Query transfers:
  GET /api/v1/site-transfers/status/PENDING
  GET /api/v1/site-transfers/receiving-site/{siteName}

  Step 8: Manage Payables

  Create payable (financial obligation):
  POST /api/v1/payables
  {
    "contractorName": "ABC Suppliers",
    "contractType": "MATERIAL",
    "amountRecorded": 45000.00,
    "amountPaid": 20000.00,
    "vendorId": 1,
    "goodsReceivedNoteId": 1
  }

  Query payables:
  GET /api/v1/payables                        # All payables
  GET /api/v1/payables/vendor/{vendorId}
  GET /api/v1/payables/grn/{grnId}

  Key Features

  1. Automatic Inventory Management

  - No manual stock updates needed
  - Event-driven architecture ensures consistency
  - Complete audit trail via InventoryTransaction records

  2. Stock Validation

  - InventoryService validates sufficient stock before consumption/transfer
  - Throws InsufficientStockException with detailed error messages
  - Prevents negative inventory

  3. Traceability

  - Every inventory change links to source document (GRN number, transfer number, etc.)
  - Complete chain from Indent → PO → GRN → Inventory → Consumption
  - IndentItem tracks conversion to PO and links to PO number

  4. Purchase Order Tracking

  - Tracks ordered vs received quantities per item
  - Automatic status updates (PARTIALLY_RECEIVED/FULLY_RECEIVED)
  - Links back to Indent for requisition tracking

  5. Financial Integration

  - Payables link GRN to vendor payments
  - Tracks amount due calculation: amountRecorded - amountPaid
  - Supports different contract types

  System Architecture Highlights

  Event-Driven Design:
  - Services publish events (GrnCreatedEvent, MaterialConsumedEvent, etc.)
  - InventoryEventListener handles inventory updates asynchronously
  - Ensures loose coupling and transaction safety (AFTER_COMMIT phase)

  Data Integrity:
  - Transaction management ensures atomicity
  - Validation before stock movements
  - Unique constraints on document numbers

  Query Flexibility:
  - Filter by date range, vendor, status, material
  - Pagination support for large datasets
  - Search capabilities for materials

  File Structure

  goodsReceivedNote/     - GRN management
  grnItem/               - GRN line items
  indentItem/            - Indent line items
  intend/                - Material requisitions
  inventoryTransaction/  - Inventory ledger (auto-generated)
  material/              - Material master
  materialConsumption/   - Usage records
  payable/               - Financial obligations
  purchaseOrder/         - PO management
  purchaseOrderItem/     - PO line items
  siteTransfer/          - Inter-site transfers
  siteTransferItem/      - Transfer line items
  vendor/                - Vendor master

  Each module follows standard structure: Entity, Repository, Service, Controller, DTOs, and Enums.

  The system provides a complete, traceable procurement-to-consumption workflow with automated inventory management and strong data integrity.
